From: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Subject: net: ethernet: mtk_wed: fix wdma rx hang on wed after SER

Backport of hunk 1 of MTK SDK patch
"[PATCH 03/15] fix wdma rx hang on wed1 after SER"
(999-wed-03-fix-wdma-rx-hang-on-wed1-after-SER, recover the original via
`git show eef2a51256:target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/...`).

The desc check in mtk_wdma_rx_reset() is inverted: the CPU_IDX zeroing
is applied only to rings that have NO descriptors, so every *active*
WDMA RX ring comes out of an SER reset with a stale CPU index and the
WDMA RX side resumes mid-ring. Verified still inverted in both vanilla
6.12.87 and mainline master as of 2026-07-10 — never upstreamed.

Motivation on this box: 2026-07-10 SER quiesce test wedged the mt7915
MCU (FW_LOG_2_HOST 0x13ed timeout, mt7915_mac_full_reset 10x loop);
mtk_wdma_rx_reset() runs inside that recovery path (breadcrumb id 32).
See docs/WED-breadcrumb-harness-design.md "SER patch re-audit".

Adaptation: hunk 2 of the SDK patch (WDMA RX prefetch SIDX/FIFO clears)
is dropped — MTK_WED_WDMA_RX_PREF_CFG is v3-only hardware; MT7622 is
WED v1.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
@@ -361,7 +361,7 @@ mtk_wdma_rx_reset(struct mtk_wed_device
 	wdma_w32(dev, MTK_WDMA_RESET_IDX, 0);

 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->rx_wdma); i++) {
-		if (dev->rx_wdma[i].desc)
+		if (!dev->rx_wdma[i].desc)
 			continue;

 		wdma_w32(dev,
